{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/43901-slices-of-self-importance-jimb-s-essay-journal","id":43901,"title":"Slices of Self-Importance: JimB's Essay Journal","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-06T19:50:19-08:00","id":43901,"title":"Slices of Self-Importance: JimB's Essay Journal","content":"My dad is tired of working for the city of Mexico, so he put in for Social Security retirement benefits. He almost didn't. He already has retirement from something like thirty years working for the city of Columbia, and the couple of years he spent at Mexico would net him only about a hundred bucks a month. My dad is very much the kind of guy who would rather not have $1,200 per year than fill out paperwork.<br /> <br /> But he went ahead and filled out the paperwork, and when he did, an error that would have never been otherwise caught was brought to Social Security's attention: They had forgotten to pay him the death benefits of my mom's retirement. They hadn't made one payment in the six years since she'd died. Next month, they will be sending him a check for what they owe him, which works out to just shy of twenty thousand dollars. He has decided to take the family on a vacation, maybe to Hawaii but wherever my sister decides because he has delegated all the planning to her, which I think proves my point about what he would do to avoid paperwork.<br /> <br /> In preparation for this event, I have decided to resurrect my old essay journal, which was only ever good when it was a travel blog anyway. I am cynically looking forward to taking a trip with my blood family and my sister's secret girlfriend to a place where gay people are allowed to marry, which trip shall consist of at least two plane rides with a six-month-old baby. It is not impossible that I will be shot by an air marshal for trying to bring the plane down, though for the record, that attempted mass murder will, in my eyes, be an act of self-defense. If it happens, I'm sure you'll hear about it in the news.<br /> <br /> The trip won't be for a while. I don't know when. We kids would like to convince Dad not to spend his money until he's cashed the check, but he wants to get to Hawaii while it's still cold in Missouri (and it is cold, colder than a drowned well-digger), which I have to admit is an idea I see the attraction of. Never mind. The point is, I'm really jumping the gun by restarting this thing, but hey, fuck it, I always liked having a place to tell stories. Perhaps I will warm up by telling you of my hunt for a unicorn in the fabled Kingdom City.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T04:51:29-08:00","id":44077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus <i>Lepidodactylus lugubris, </i>a species with a not-really-accurate-they're-doing-just-fine-thank-you common name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm...I can do this. &quot;Lepid&quot; implies a butterfly, and &quot;lugubris&quot; sounds like a cognate of &quot;lugubrious,&quot; and &quot;dactylus...&quot; So, it's, like, a happy pterodactyl-butterfly hybrid?<br /> <br /> Alright, fine, I'll go look it up on Wikipedia, then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user